From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: leave a program's data mapping to the host to zero

An exec mapped the program's data and bss anonymously, so nommu's
do_mmap cleared every page of it (52 of the 85 pages a BusyBox exec
zeroes), and the host then wrote the module's data image over most of
the same bytes, or copied a pristine image over all of them.

load_wasm_file now maps the data with MAP_UNINITIALIZED when the mm is
in the kernel's memory, and wasm_load_program (the new name of
wasm_load_executable, with the mapping's length as a fifth argument)
tells the host that the mapping is not zeroed, so the host writes every
byte of it before the program runs. A host without the new import
cannot instantiate the kernel, so no old host runs a program on the
bytes of another. A mm in a memory of its own (a non-root exec) is
copied to the host's memory as mapped, so it keeps the zeroing and
passes 0.

The flag needs CONFIG_MMAP_ALLOW_UNINITIALIZED, which honours it from
user space too: ksys_mmap_pgoff clears it, so a program's mmap still
returns zeroed memory. The stack and argument mappings stay zeroed.
---
--- a/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig
+++ b/arch/wasm/configs/wasm32_nommu_defconfig
@@ -56,3 +56,4 @@
 CONFIG_MULTIUSER=y
 CONFIG_POSIX_TIMERS=y
 CONFIG_CGROUPS=y
+CONFIG_MMAP_ALLOW_UNINITIALIZED=y
--- a/arch/wasm/include/asm/wasm.h
+++ b/arch/wasm/include/asm/wasm.h
@@ -19,8 +19,14 @@
 extern struct task_struct *wasm_serialize_tasks(struct task_struct *prev_task,
 	struct task_struct *next_task);
 
-extern int wasm_load_executable(unsigned long bin_start, unsigned long bin_end,
-	unsigned long data_start, unsigned long table_start);
+/*
+ * gmux: data_unzeroed is the length of the data mapping from data_start when the kernel left it
+ * as the page allocator had it (0: it is zeroed). The host writes every byte of those before the
+ * program runs. A host without this import cannot instantiate the kernel, so it never runs a
+ * program on another's bytes.
+ */
+extern int wasm_load_program(unsigned long bin_start, unsigned long bin_end,
+	unsigned long data_start, unsigned long table_start, unsigned long data_unzeroed);
 extern void wasm_reload_program(void);
 
 extern void wasm_clone_callback(void);
--- a/fs/binfmt_wasm.c
+++ b/fs/binfmt_wasm.c
@@ -429,13 +429,19 @@
 	}
 
 	/*
-	 * MAP_ANMONYMOUS clears the data (and bss). In Wasm, the runtime
-	 * manages bss inside the data area. The runtime may rely on the data
-	 * being zeroed as it is placing bss inside (or rather not touchhing bss
-	 * pages at all). Thus data and bss are the same and zeroed.
+	 * In Wasm, the runtime manages bss inside the data area, and may rely on
+	 * the data being zeroed as it is placing bss inside (or rather not
+	 * touching bss pages at all). Thus data and bss are the same and zeroed.
+	 * In the kernel's memory the host zeroes or restores every byte of the
+	 * mapping before the program runs (wasm_load_program), so the kernel
+	 * leaves it alone. A mm in a memory of its own is copied to it as
+	 * mapped, and that copy must be zeros.
 	 */
 	data_start = vm_mmap(NULL, 0, data_size,
-			PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE, MAP_PRIVATE|MAP_ANONYMOUS, 0);
+			PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE,
+			MAP_PRIVATE|MAP_ANONYMOUS|
+			(current->mm->context.private_memory ?
+				0 : MAP_UNINITIALIZED), 0);
 	if (!data_start || IS_ERR_VALUE(data_start)) {
 		ret = data_start ? (int)data_start : -ENOMEM;
 		pr_err("Unable to allocate RAM for process data, errno: %d\n",
@@ -540,8 +546,10 @@
 	 * The host refuses code it holds no build of. That is past the point
 	 * of no return, so exec kills the process with SIGSEGV.
 	 */
-	if (wasm_load_executable(current->mm->start_code, current->mm->end_code,
-			current->mm->start_data, 0U))
+	if (wasm_load_program(current->mm->start_code, current->mm->end_code,
+			current->mm->start_data, 0U,
+			current->mm->context.private_memory ? 0 :
+				current->mm->end_data - current->mm->start_data))
 		return -ENOEXEC;
 
 	finalize_exec(bprm);
--- a/mm/nommu.c
+++ b/mm/nommu.c
@@ -1339,6 +1339,8 @@
 	struct file *file = NULL;
 	unsigned long retval = -EBADF;
 
+	/* a program's anonymous memory is always zeroed; only the kernel's own mappings skip it */
+	flags &= ~MAP_UNINITIALIZED;
 	audit_mmap_fd(fd, flags);
 	if (!(flags & MAP_ANONYMOUS)) {
 		file = fget(fd);
--
2.43.0

